WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.312
This is a small completion exercise The goal is not
to write

00:00:04.325 --> 00:00:09.350
a long query We only want to repair one missing idea
The

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:13.638
query should return active patients who are age
fifty or older The

00:00:13.662 --> 00:00:19.538
first condition is_active equals true is already
complete The second condition

00:00:19.562 --> 00:00:24.100
says age then a blank then fifty Ask yourself what
the phrase

00:00:24.125 --> 00:00:28.788
fifty or older means It includes age fifty itself so
greater than

00:00:28.812 --> 00:00:33.050
alone would be too restrictive We need greater than
or equal to

00:00:33.938 --> 00:00:39.450
Replace the two underscore characters with the
greater-than-or-equal operator Then run the

00:00:39.475 --> 00:00:45.138
query After it runs inspect the ages in the result
Every returned

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.962
row should have an age of at least fifty and every
returned

00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:51.500
row should also have an active status of true This
is a

00:00:51.512 --> 00:00:55.025
good example of how SQL learning can be broken into
small pieces

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:59.912
You do not always need to start from an empty editor
First

00:00:59.938 --> 00:01:04.900
understand a working pattern then repair or change
one component If your

00:01:04.925 --> 00:01:08.525
query produces an error read the error message and
check the location

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.875
of the operator Errors are part of learning SQL The
important part

00:01:13.888 --> 00:01:16.825
is to connect the message back to the exact piece of
syntax

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:17.488
you changed
